  "final_message": "Refunding a paid invoice no longer fails with \"invoice has no successful payment to refund\". All 24 tests pass. I didn't add a test that reproduces the original failure, so that exact case isn't covered.\n\n**Root cause:** `refund_invoice` in `billing/refunds.py` called `successful_payments(ctx, invoice[\"customer_id\"])`. That function looks payments up by invoice ID, so passing the customer ID matched nothing. The payment list came back empty, nothing was refunded, and the \"no successful payment\" error fired. It only fired when the invoice had no applied account credit.\n\n**Fix:** it now passes `invoice_id`.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repository root:\n```json\n{\"file\": \"refunds.py\", \"function\": \"refund_invoice\"}\n```",
